WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.330
Speaker 1: You know, one of the questions
we've been asking during this historic anti-vaccine

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:11.599
era around the world because of the COVID
vaccines, is is it going to is anti-vax going

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:19.350
to start to bleed over to more general vaccine
opposition, not just the COVID vaccine?

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.380
What about measles?

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.640
What about MMR and others?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.510
And so far, the answer appears to be unfortunately
yes.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.810
And this was very predictable.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.510
There's a good article in The Guardian.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:36.470
Measles cases surge nearly 80% in the wake
of COVID chaos, with fears other diseases

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.040
could follow.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.980
UNICEF says virus is canary in the coal mine
that shows up.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.300
I think I think it's supposed to say shows
us the gaps in vaccination campaigns for preventable

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.300
illness.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.960
Measles cases have surged nearly 80% worldwide
amid disruption caused by COVID.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:59.180
The UN says the coronavirus pandemic has interrupted
vaccination campaigns for non-covid diseases

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:03.680
around the world, creating a perfect storm
that could put millions of children's lives

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.250
at risk.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:10.410
A measles is a disease caused by a virus that
attacks mainly children.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.000
Vaccination uptake of at least 95% is the
way to avoid it spreading.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.760
Some countries fall short of that goal.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.330
Somalia at just 46%.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.580
There's also concerns about whether yellow
fever could surge.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:31.420
There are concerns about the Ukrainian invasion
by Russia and the effect that that could have.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:38.290
The U.N. says 57 vaccination campaigns in
43 countries have been postponed.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.370
So this is focusing on access.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:48.860
But the problem is we saw outbreaks in the
United States of measles before the COVID

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.860
pandemic.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.780
So the point here is basically twofold.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:58.250
Because of the pandemic, there have been campaigns
of vaccination that have been interrupted.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.960
And they tell us how quickly you can see outbreaks
of something as contagious as measles, which

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.530
in particular is a problem among children
in the United States.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:16.430
A big sort of battle line on the anti-vax
front is the vaccination of children.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:21.450
Before we even had the COVID vaccines in this
controversy, we had some pretty good sized

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.140
measles outbreaks.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.020
There was the Disneyland one in California.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:29.430
There were some religious sects in New York
City where we were seeing outbreaks.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.860
There was one in Italy, a couple others that
I can't remember.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:38.510
These outbreaks were in part based on the
idea that parents didn't want to vaccinate

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.510
their kids.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.790
Now, with measles, understand how critical
that is, particularly when it's so contagious

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.540
that you need to be vaccinating 95%.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:53.230
It is a concern right now that we are going
to start seeing as more and more kids come

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:58.160
up for vaccination boosters, for other diseases,
or as more and more kids are born and it's

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.910
time for them to get the shots that babies
get in the first six months.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:08.520
We are almost certainly going to see some
more general vaccine hesitancy on the basis

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.700
of COVID vaccine hesitancy, and it's going
to lead to more of some of these diseases.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:19.599
And the measles pre-COVID example is one of
the best ones, just small areas where they

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:23.489
said, I don't I don't want to vaccinate my
kid against measles.

00:03:23.489 --> 00:03:24.700
And they had outbreaks.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.849
And it's very serious for kids.

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:29.860
It could get very, very bad.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:35.080
And so while on the one hand, we're fighting
the vaccination battle on COVID, specifically,

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.569
there's this other more general Anti-Vaxx
thing that is beneath the surface.

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:42.819
And we've heard from some mean, you know,
look at the interviews we've seen from Trump

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:46.910
rallies where parents say, well, it's it's
not just the COVID vaccine.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.310
I'm getting my kids off of all of these vaccines.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:52.170
There is sometimes they call them, they say
they're injections.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.849
They're not, strictly speaking, vaccines.

00:03:55.849 --> 00:03:57.940
This could get very bad very quickly.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.209
And we should be paying close attention to
the numbers from all over the world.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:05.230
We'll have more about this story on our Instagram.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.050
Make sure you're following us there at David
Pakman show.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.180
We'll take a quick break.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.120
We'll look at the White House Correspondents
Dinner.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.370
We'll look at a few other things.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:12.460
Be right back.

